 "_": "Criterion 3 clause F -- the decomposition that attributes the residual contemporaneous bias to a NAMED lever. Committed 08-09-2026.",
 "the_lever": "[R-ANCHOR-01 CLAUSE THREE] -- a forecast rate that climbs past everything the company has ever FILED is a claim, named and sourced from a closed list of mechanisms. A MECHANICAL LENS CANNOT NAME ONE BY CONSTRUCTION: it is forbidden judgement drivers, and a mechanism is a judgement. So a mechanical projection rising past the filed record is asserting something nothing in it is entitled to assert, and that is a lever with a standing rule and a gate behind it rather than a parameter somebody chose.",
 "what_this_is_not": "IT IS AN ATTRIBUTION, NEVER A PROMOTED LEVER. The pre-registration fixes six levers in order before any score existed and this is not among them; the same distinction this lens already draws around its unit-error readings. NOTHING HERE MOVES A PUBLISHED FAIR VALUE.",
 "point_in_time": "The peak is AS AT THE ORIGIN, never as at today -- a later good year must not license an earlier forecast that could not have known about it.",
